{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And I pleaded with YHWH at that time, saying</b> — Since he mentioned the conquest of the land of Sihon and Og and said (Deuteronomy 3:21), 'And I commanded Joshua at that time,' he mentioned that I myself will not pass there, for I pleaded with HaShem the honored One and He did not listen to me, and He commanded me to strengthen Joshua for he will pass over. And the reason for 'at that time' is a hint to the time of the decree which he mentioned (Deuteronomy 1:37), 'Also with me HaShem was angry,' and there the supplication on the day of the event was not mentioned. And the correct interpretation is that <b>at that time</b> means at the time mentioned, when I conquered Sihon and Og and began to wage war against the nations that were given to Israel and I divided the land to the two tribes, and this was when it was said to him (Numbers 27:12), 'Go up to this mountain of Avarim,' for then he sought mercy for the matter and pleaded this supplication, and when HaShem did not listen to his voice he turned again and prayed, 'Let YHWH, the Elohim of the spirits of all flesh, appoint a man over the congregation,' as is mentioned there (Deuteronomy 3:16), and this is 'And command Joshua' (Deuteronomy 3:28). But there he mentioned the prayer that was answered, whereas here he mentioned this to make known that the land was very beloved to him and he did not merit it on their account, and all this is part of his reproofs."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:13:54.310226444Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}